# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
#
# Trivy vulnerability suppressions (06 §5.5). Every entry is:
#
#   <CVE-ID> exp:YYYY-MM-DD  ## expires: YYYY-MM-DD — one-line reason
#
# `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` is trivy's own syntax — it stops honoring the suppression
# after that date, so the finding comes back on its own rather than staying
# silenced forever. `## expires: ...` restates the same date in a form
# `trivy-fs`'s own CI step also greps for, as a second, tool-independent
# tripwire. A suppression is a snooze, not a decision.

# js-yaml 4.2.0 (CVE-2026-59869, CVE-2026-84375, GHSA-5p4m-2wfm-xmqj: YAML
# parser DoS / quadratic-CPU findings) — transitive via
# @hey-api/json-schema-ref-parser <- @hey-api/openapi-ts, a WP 0.5
# (apps/web) build-time OpenAPI codegen devDependency. It never reaches any
# image WP 0.4 builds: docker/api.Dockerfile's `pnpm install --prod
# --filter-prod=@app/api...` excludes devDependencies and `rm -rf apps/web`
# entirely (verified — see docs/evidence/phase-0/wp0.4-container-hardening.md).
# js-yaml's three advisories (snoozed 2026-09-12, due 2026-10-12) were closed on
# 2026-10-05 by a lockfile bump to js-yaml 4.3.2 (devDependency, never shipped).

# personalfi/proxy's `usr/bin/caddy` binary (gobinary scanner): the 16 Go-module
# and stdlib findings snoozed 2026-09-12, re-snoozed 2026-09-26 and due 2026-10-10
# were CLOSED on 2026-10-05 by an upstream rebuild — caddy:2-alpine v2.11.6
# (sha256:d44355d3…) carries none of them, nor any other HIGH/CRITICAL with a fix
# available (trivy 0.74.0: 28 → 0 on the base image, 0 on the rebuilt proxy
# image). docker/caddy.Dockerfile's pin was bumped; no xcaddy build was needed.
# Renovate watches the digest from here.
# source-map-js 1.2.1 (CVE-2026-93749): snoozed 2026-10-06 while the fix sat
# inside minimumReleaseAge; CLOSED 2026-10-07 by the lockfile bump to 1.2.2
# (pnpm-workspace.yaml override). No suppression remains.

# personalfi/proxy's `usr/bin/caddy` (gobinary): three Go DoS findings published
# after the Phase 9 gate's green run at 14c391f (2026-10-08) — CVE-2026-78667
# (net/http, crafted request), CVE-2026-78669 (x/net http2 and stdlib: HTTP/2
# SETTINGS flood) and CVE-2026-97031 (crypto/tls). Fixed in Go 1.26.9 / 1.27.2
# and x/net 0.60.0; upstream caddy:2-alpine v2.11.7 (2026-10-05,
# sha256:d8542f48…) still ships the vulnerable build, so there is no digest to
# bump to. Residual: denial of service only, against a proxy bound to the LAN
# or Tailscale (never the internet) — no confidentiality or integrity path.
# Snoozed 2026-10-10 for four weeks; the bump to the first upstream release
# that clears them is the procedure in RUNBOOK "Upgrading the image" (Renovate
# watches the digest). If none exists by the expiry, build caddy with xcaddy on
# a patched Go, the fallback 09 reserved.
CVE-2026-78667 exp:2026-11-07  ## expires: 2026-11-07 — caddy gobinary net/http DoS; no upstream build clears it yet
CVE-2026-78669 exp:2026-11-07  ## expires: 2026-11-07 — caddy gobinary x/net+stdlib HTTP/2 SETTINGS DoS; no upstream build clears it yet
CVE-2026-97031 exp:2026-11-07  ## expires: 2026-11-07 — caddy gobinary crypto/tls DoS; no upstream build clears it yet
CVE-2026-111943 exp:2026-11-07  ## expires: 2026-11-07 — caddy gobinary crypto/x509 MITM (Go stdlib < 1.26.10 / 1.27.3); caddy:2.11.7-alpine (the newest, 2026-10-03) still ships Go 1.26.8 — no upstream build clears it yet; re-rule with the other three on expiry
CVE-2026-116587 exp:2026-11-07  ## expires: 2026-11-07 — caddy gobinary go-jose/v4 JWK-parsing DoS (fixed in 4.1.6); caddy:2.11.7-alpine (the newest) still vendors 4.1.5 — no upstream build clears it yet; re-rule with the other four on expiry, or build Caddy from source with patched modules (queued)
CVE-2026-56857 exp:2026-11-07  ## expires: 2026-11-07 — caddy gobinary Go stdlib os.Root.Mkdir(All) follows junctions out of the root ON WINDOWS ONLY (fixed in 1.26.9 / 1.27.2); the proxy is a Linux alpine container with no Windows junctions and Caddy does not expose os.Root to any input, so there is no path here; caddy:2.11.7-alpine as rebuilt 2026-10-22 (sha256:eb4d35b7…) still ships Go 1.26.8 and adds alpine brotli/curl findings of its own, so no digest to bump to — re-rule with the other five on expiry (xcaddy on a patched Go is the queued fallback)
